{
  "slug": "presente-regular",
  "number": 4,
  "part": 1,
  "level": "A1",
  "title": "The regular present",
  "tagline": "-ar, -er and -ir verbs, and why Spanish can drop «I» and «you».",
  "goal": "Conjugate any regular verb in the present, drop the subject pronoun like native speakers do, and use the present for habits, facts and the near future.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "terminaciones",
      "title": "Three families of verbs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Every Spanish infinitive ends in **-ar**, **-er** or **-ir**. Remove the ending and add the endings of the person:"
        },
        {
          "type": "conjugation",
          "persons": ["yo", "tú", "él / ella / usted", "nosotros", "ellos / ellas / ustedes"],
          "verbs": [
            { "verb": "hablar", "meaning": "to speak", "forms": ["habl{o}", "habl{as}", "habl{a}", "habl{amos}", "habl{an}"] },
            { "verb": "comer", "meaning": "to eat", "forms": ["com{o}", "com{es}", "com{e}", "com{emos}", "com{en}"] },
            { "verb": "vivir", "meaning": "to live", "forms": ["viv{o}", "viv{es}", "viv{e}", "viv{imos}", "viv{en}"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "tip",
          "text": "-er and -ir verbs are identical except for *nosotros*: *comemos* / *vivimos*."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sujeto",
      "title": "No need for «I» or «you»",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The ending already says who does the action, so Spanish usually **drops the subject pronoun**: *Hablo español* = I speak Spanish. Using *yo*, *tú*… adds emphasis or contrast."
        },
        {
          "type": "examples",
          "items": [
            { "fr": "{Trabajo} en una oficina.", "tr": "I work in an office." },
            { "fr": "¿{Vives} aquí?", "tr": "Do you live here?" },
            { "fr": "Yo {cocino} y tú {lavas} los platos.", "tr": "I cook and YOU wash the dishes.", "note": "contrast" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "text": "No «do / does» in questions or negatives: *¿Hablas inglés?* (Do you speak English?) · *No como carne* (I don't eat meat)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "usos",
      "title": "What the present is for",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Use", "Example", "English"],
          "rows": [
            ["Habits and facts", "*{Desayuno} a las siete.*", "I have breakfast at seven."],
            ["Right now (also estar + -ando)", "*¿Qué {haces}?*", "What are you doing?"],
            ["Near future, with a time word", "*Mañana {trabajo}.*", "I'm working tomorrow."],
            ["How long (with desde hace)", "*{Vivo} aquí desde hace un año.*", "I've lived here for a year."]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "conjuga",
      "section": "terminaciones",
      "title": "Conjugate",
      "instructions": "Write the verb in the present.",
      "kind": "type",
      "items": [
        { "prompt": "Yo ___ español. (hablar)", "answer": "hablo" },
        { "prompt": "Tú ___ mucho. (trabajar)", "answer": "trabajas" },
        { "prompt": "Ella ___ en Bogotá. (vivir)", "answer": "vive" },
        { "prompt": "Nosotros ___ a las dos. (comer)", "answer": "comemos" },
        { "prompt": "Ustedes ___ el periódico. (leer)", "answer": "leen" },
        { "prompt": "Nosotros ___ en un departamento. (vivir)", "answer": "vivimos" },
        { "prompt": "Él ___ cartas. (escribir)", "answer": "escribe" },
        { "prompt": "Yo ___ café todas las mañanas. (tomar)", "answer": "tomo" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "quien",
      "section": "sujeto",
      "title": "Who is it?",
      "instructions": "No pronoun in the sentence: who is doing the action?",
      "kind": "choice",
      "options": ["yo", "tú", "él / ella", "nosotros", "ellos"],
      "speak": "prompt",
      "items": [
        { "prompt": "Bailamos salsa los viernes.", "answer": "nosotros" },
        { "prompt": "Cocino muy bien.", "answer": "yo" },
        { "prompt": "¿Comes carne?", "answer": "tú" },
        { "prompt": "Viven en Lima.", "answer": "ellos" },
        { "prompt": "Escribe un correo.", "answer": "él / ella" },
        { "prompt": "Estudiamos español.", "answer": "nosotros" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "orden",
      "section": "usos",
      "title": "Build the sentence",
      "instructions": "Put the words in order.",
      "kind": "order",
      "speak": "answer",
      "items": [
        { "words": ["no", "como", "carne"], "answer": "no como carne" },
        { "words": ["¿hablas", "inglés?"], "answer": "¿hablas inglés?" },
        { "words": ["mañana", "trabajo", "en", "casa"], "answer": "mañana trabajo en casa" },
        { "words": ["vivo", "aquí", "desde", "hace", "un", "año"], "answer": "vivo aquí desde hace un año" },
        { "words": ["desayunamos", "a", "las", "siete"], "answer": "desayunamos a las siete" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "traduce",
      "section": "final",
      "title": "Say it in Spanish",
      "instructions": "Translate. Leave out the subject pronoun.",
      "kind": "type",
      "speak": "answer",
      "items": [
        { "prompt": "I live in Mexico.", "answer": "Vivo en México." },
        { "prompt": "Do you speak Spanish? (tú)", "answer": "¿Hablas español?" },
        { "prompt": "We don't eat meat.", "answer": "No comemos carne." },
        { "prompt": "They work on Saturdays.", "answer": "Trabajan los sábados." },
        { "prompt": "I'm working tomorrow.", "answer": "Mañana trabajo.", "accept": ["Trabajo mañana."] },
        { "prompt": "She reads a lot.", "answer": "Lee mucho.", "accept": ["Ella lee mucho."] }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "checklist": [
    "I conjugate regular -ar, -er and -ir verbs in the present.",
    "I drop yo, tú… when they aren't needed.",
    "I make questions and negatives without «do».",
    "I use the present for habits and the near future."
  ],
  "challenge": {
    "title": "A typical week",
    "text": "Write six sentences about your week with six different regular verbs and no subject pronouns: *Trabajo de lunes a viernes. Los martes cocino con mi pareja. Los sábados corro en el parque.*"
  }
}
